# Chroma library, modern Earth: INNER DRIVERS across stages (states that build up and push the person to act). Plan: earth-plan.md "Across stages".
# Syntax: header of build.py. Each driver is even on its own: alpha even, the five one-color options and one full cross cycle (s1 to s4 spread evenly).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- painful and draining states

== the same week, over and over
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: mixed
life: work, school, home
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague, a neighbour
earth: the same alarm, the same bus, the same tasks, and a flat grey feeling that nothing new will ever happen
requires: twelve or more ordinary weeks in a row (no life event, no new commitment, no move), and meaning below 0.45 or competence unchanged over the whole stretch
likelier: juvenile and young adult years; a routine job or a long school term; autonomy below 0.4 (little say over the day); retirement without plans; much Red in the color history
rarer: an absorbing hobby or plan; a new child, job or move within the year; a goal the routine clearly serves; high steadiness
times: Most people, a stretch or two a year, at any age from the teens on (estimate)
gap: 0-0.5
scene: The alarm, the bus, the same desk, the same voices. Halfway through the morning {N} notices they have been staring at the clock for ten minutes.
scene W: {N} keeps to the timetable as always, but lately the duties feel like a coat gone thin at the elbows.
scene U: {Ns} mind wanders off for the third time this hour, and {N} starts to wonder what exactly it is looking for.
scene B: {N} looks round at the same faces doing the same things and thinks: nobody gets anywhere like this.
scene R: {Ns} legs jiggle under the desk. Every part of {N} wants to stand up, walk out and do something, anything.
scene G: The days come round like the same leaf turning in the same eddy. {N} wonders whether this is a season or a whole life.
- W | do every dull task properly, and take pride in a job done right | habit | v: conformity, achievement | chance: 78
- U | make a game of the routine: time yourself, and beat yesterday's record | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 82
- B | trade a favour to get someone else to do the dull part | v: power, hedonism | chance: 82
- R | drop it all for an afternoon and go somewhere you have never been | v: stimulation | closed: approval: skipping school or work; backfire: missed, and in trouble for it | chance: 85
- G | stop fighting it: look out of the window and let the hours drift by | v: none clear (letting time pass) | chance: 58
- W>U | ask whoever is in charge to let you learn a new part of the work | door | v: self-direction, conformity | mark: learned a skill | act: ask whoever is in charge to let them learn a new part of the work | chance: 64
- U>B | find a way to finish the routine in half the time, and keep the rest | v: achievement, hedonism | closed: approval: idling on paid or set time; backfire: found out, and given twice the work | chance: 70
- B>R | stir up a little trouble between two others, just to see what happens | v: stimulation | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: mischief-making; backfire: found out, and left out | chance: 69
- R>G | get outside and run, climb or swim until the heaviness lifts | body: light | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 90
- G>W | join the neighbours who tend the shared garden every Saturday | door | habit | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 82
works: By the end of the month {N} has something to look forward to on Thursdays.
works: The days are still the same days, but {N} no longer counts the minutes.
fails: Nothing changes, and the grey weeks roll on.
fails: The attempt goes wrong, and {N} ends up in trouble as well as bored.

== a friend's good news stings
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: friends, work, school
horizon: week
roles: friend, sibling, colleague
earth: a friend of your own age gets the prize, the promotion, the house or the baby you wanted, and everyone is congratulating them
requires: a friend, sibling or colleague within about five years of the person's age had a success within the last three months (a prize, a place, a promotion, a wedding, a baby, a house) in a field where the person's own competence is below 0.5
likelier: the two are alike in age, sex and path; the person's own standing is low or falling; juvenile and young adult years; a week of scrolling through other people's highlights; much Black in the color history
rarer: with age (envy falls after fifty); satisfaction above 0.65; gratitude acts within the year; the success is in a field the person does not care about
times: Nearly everyone, a few times a year, most sharply between friends of the same age (estimate)
gap: 0-0.5
scene: {friend} has the thing {N} wanted, and everyone is congratulating them. {N} smiles along, and something small and sour turns over inside.
scene W: {N} knows {friend} earned it fairly, and is ashamed of the sour feeling. A good friend should only be glad.
scene U: {N} keeps going over it: what did {friend} do differently, and where exactly did {N} fall behind?
scene B: It should have been {Ns}. {N} watches {friend} take the applause and starts counting what {friend} has that {N} does not.
scene R: The smile hurts. {N} wants to shout, or cry, or both, and leaves the room before it shows.
scene G: Some trees grow faster than others in the same soil. {N} tells themselves this, and does not quite believe it yet.
- W | congratulate them warmly, and keep the sour feeling to yourself | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 80
- U | ask them how they did it, step by step, and take notes | door | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 80
- B | decide you will have the same within a year, and start working for it | v: achievement | chance: 50
- R | admit your jealousy to them out loud, and laugh about it together | v: benevolence | mark: owned up | chance: 78
- G | stop scrolling, count what is good in your own life, and let it settle | habit | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 90
- W>B | ask the people who decide what it takes to be picked next time | v: achievement, power | chance: 68
- U>R | work out what they did, then try something bolder they would never dare | v: stimulation, achievement | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 55
- B>G | avoid them for a while and unfollow them, until it stops hurting | v: security | chance: 88
- R>W | lead the cheering for them, louder than anyone, in front of everyone | v: benevolence | chance: 78
- G>U | go back to what you are naturally good at, and grow it patiently | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 78
works: The sting fades, and {N} can look {friend} in the eye again.
works: {N} turns the feeling into a push, and gets somewhere of their own.
fails: The sourness stays, and every new piece of good news makes it worse.
fails: Something {N} said gets back to {friend}, and things between them go cold.

== guilt that will not go away
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: friends, family, faith
horizon: months
roles: friend, sibling, parent, an elder
earth: something you did, or failed to do, weeks ago, and nobody mentions it, but you cannot stop thinking about it
requires: a mark 'broke your word', 'hid a wrong' or 'refused someone in need' within the last two years, or an act against the ends the person holds most that hurt someone close; and peace below 0.45 for four weeks or more
likelier: much White or Green in the color history (benevolence, conformity, tradition ranked high); the person wronged is close and still around; reactivity above 1; a faith commitment held
rarer: the harm was small or shared; the person owned up at the time; much Black in the color history; the person wronged has moved away or died long ago
times: Most people, a guilt that lingers for weeks every year or two (estimate)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: It was weeks ago, and nobody mentions it any more. But {N} keeps coming back to it at night, the way a tongue goes back to a broken tooth.
scene W: {N} knows exactly what was owed and was not given. The knowledge sits like a stone in a pocket, heavier every day.
scene U: {N} replays it again: the moment, the choice, what should have been said instead. The replay never changes the ending.
scene B: {N} tells themselves it is done, it is over, everyone does such things. The thought will not stay down.
scene R: Every time {N} sees {friend}, {Ns} face goes hot and {N} has to look away.
scene G: The wrong has put down roots. {N} feels it under everything, the way damp gets into the walls of a house.
- W | confess it to a parent, an elder or a priest, and make the amends they ask | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 82
- U | write it all down, honestly, until you understand why you did it | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- B | decide guilt is a leash other people hold, and stop wearing it | identity | v: self-direction, power | chance: 65
- R | go round tonight and pour the whole thing out, tears and all | v: benevolence | mark: owned up | chance: 78
- G | accept that it happened, carry it quietly, and be kinder from now on | v: benevolence, tradition (humility) | chance: 69
- W>R | own up to whoever is in charge and take the punishment, to be free of it | v: conformity | mark: owned up | identity | chance: 78
- U>G | find a quiet way to repair the harm, and never say who caused it | v: benevolence | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 75
- B>W | give money to a good cause until the feeling eases | v: universalism | tags: pay:money-.05 | chance: 70
- R>U | cry it out fully, then sit down and work out what the lesson is | v: self-direction | chance: 75
- G>B | keep away from the one you hurt, and let time bury it | v: security | chance: 48
works: The weight lifts, a little at first, then for good.
works: {N} faces it, and the person {N} wronged is gentler than {N} feared.
fails: The guilt stays, and leaks into everything {N} does.
fails: Trying to set it right opens the wound again, for both of them.

== shame after a public failure
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: school, work, community
horizon: months
roles: friend, rival, boss, parent
earth: everyone saw you fail, and now you feel their eyes on you everywhere you go
requires: a failure seen by others within the last month (an exam failed, a job lost, a debt or a secret come out, a collapse on stage or on the pitch), and competence or belonging below 0.4
likelier: reactivity above 1.2; much White in the color history (honour and face matter); juvenile years; harsh critics at home; outlook below 0.4
rarer: unconditional support (ties and belonging above 0.6); a forgiving community; steadiness above 1; the failure stayed private
times: Most people, every few years, most often in the teens and twenties (estimate)
gap: 2-4
scene: Everyone saw. {N} walks past the people who saw and feels their eyes on the back of {Ns} neck, though nobody is looking.
scene W: {N} let everyone down, in front of everyone. {N} cannot stop imagining what they all say about it now.
scene U: {N} goes over the failure again and again, searching for the exact moment it went wrong, and finds a dozen.
scene B: {N} hates that they saw it. Weakness shown is weakness used, and {N} knows exactly who will use it.
scene R: The memory comes back in hot flashes, in the shower, on the stairs, and each time {N} wants to hit something or hide.
scene G: {N} feels small, like a stunted plant beside the others in the row, and wants to be left alone in the shade.
- W | apologise to those you let down, and work twice as hard to win back their trust | v: conformity, achievement | habit | chance: 75
- U | work out precisely what went wrong, and practise until it cannot happen again | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
- B | say nothing, work like mad, and win so big next time that they forget | v: achievement, power (face) | chance: 50
- R | make a joke of it, loudly, before anyone else can | v: none clear (laughing it off) | chance: 72
- G | keep your head down, stay home a while, and let the talk die away | v: security, tradition (humility) | chance: 70
- W>G | own it in front of everyone, and ask for their forgiveness | identity | v: benevolence, tradition (humility) | mark: owned up | chance: 75
- U>W | rehearse in secret for months, and come back word-perfect for the next try | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 75
- B>U | change school, club or job, and start again where nobody knows | door | v: self-direction | chance: 75
- R>B | lash out at the one who made it public | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: a scene; backfire: more people see it | chance: 35
- G>R | go off alone into the hills or the park and shout it out of your body | body: light | v: none clear (feeling let out) | chance: 71
works: The talk dies down, and {N} finds they can walk into the room again.
works: The next chance comes, and this time {N} gets it right.
fails: The failure follows {N} around for months, like a nickname that will not wear off.
fails: {N} hides from everyone, and the hiding becomes its own trouble.

== the itch to be somewhere else
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 15-110
tone: mixed
life: home, leisure, work
horizon: months
roles: friend, sibling, partner, parent
earth: a plane overhead, a postcard from a friend, and suddenly the street outside looks too small
requires: the same town, home and job or school for five years or more with no new role, and autonomy or meaning below 0.45; or an age ending in 9 or 0; or a friend or sibling who made a big move within the year
likelier: ages ending in 9; much Red or Black in the color history (stimulation and self-direction ranked high); a child left home within the year; freedom above 0.6; just after New Year or a birthday
rarer: a new role, child or project within the year; much White or Green in the color history (security and tradition ranked high); money below 0.2
times: Most people, about once a year, more at round birthdays; about 1 in 6 adults worldwide say they would move abroad if they could (Gallup)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: A plane crosses the sky over {Ns} street. {N} watches it until it is gone, and goes on standing there afterwards.
scene W: {N} has a good life here, people who count on them, and a list of reasons to stay. Lately the list has stopped working.
scene U: {N} has started reading about other cities late at night: rents, jobs, languages, how long the winters last.
scene B: Everyone who got anywhere left this town. {N} looks at the ones who stayed and does not want to be one of them.
scene R: {Ns} feet itch. A song on the radio, the smell of diesel at the station, and {N} wants to be gone by morning.
scene G: Birds leave every autumn without asking anyone. {N} feels the same tug, and wonders whether it means go or wait.
- W | talk it through with the family, and agree on a trip everyone can live with | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 78
- U | research three places properly, visit the best one, then decide | v: self-direction, security | chance: 82
- B | apply for jobs or courses elsewhere, and tell nobody until it is settled | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: moved away | chance: 65
- R | pack one bag and take the next train out, just to see | door | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 88
- G | wait until the urge has lasted a whole season; only then trust it | v: security, tradition (humility) | chance: 68
- W>U | sign up for an official exchange or posting through work or school | door | v: self-direction, conformity | chance: 68
- U>B | work out where you would get on fastest, and commit to moving there | binds | v: achievement, power (resources) | mark: moved away | chance: 68
- B>R | blow your savings on a ticket somewhere far, and stay until the money runs out | identity | v: stimulation, hedonism | mark: left home | chance: 80
- R>G | walk out of town on foot, and sleep under the open sky for a few nights | body: light | v: universalism (nature), stimulation | chance: 90
- G>W | go back to where your family came from, and help out there for a summer | door | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 78
works: {N} goes, and comes back to find the old street looking new again.
works: The plan takes shape, and the itch turns into a date on the calendar.
fails: Nothing comes of it, and the itch turns sour.
fails: {N} goes, and finds the same restlessness waiting at the other end.

== running on empty
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 18-90
tone: trouble
life: work, family, body
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, partner, child
earth: weeks of early starts and late nights, and this morning you sat in the car for ten minutes before you could make yourself go in
requires: stress above 1.5 for twelve weeks or more, with time below 0.2 and no week of rest; plus autonomy below 0.4 or a clash between what the job demands and the ends the person holds most
likelier: a caring job, or caring for a parent or a sick child; career and children held at once; much White in the color history (cannot say no) or much Blue (perfectionism); unfair treatment at work
rarer: autonomy above 0.6; a supportive partner or team (ties above 0.6); firm limits on hours; satisfaction above 0.65
times: Many working adults, a breaking point every year or two in hard stretches; about 2 in 3 US workers feel burned out at least sometimes (Gallup 2018)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: {N} sits in the parked car outside work for ten minutes, engine off, unable to make the hand open the door.
scene W: So many people are counting on {N}. {N} cannot let them down, and cannot remember the last time {N} slept through the night.
scene U: {N} reads the same sentence four times and it still will not go in. The mind {N} always relied on has turned to fog.
scene B: {N} has given this place everything, and {boss} still asks for more. {N} starts to wonder what all of it is buying.
scene R: {N} snaps at {colleague} over nothing, and then cannot stop crying in the toilets.
scene G: {N} feels like a field farmed too many seasons without rest. Nothing more will grow until something is left fallow.
- W | ask formally for lighter duties, and hold the line once it is agreed | v: security, conformity | chance: 68
- U | log every hour for a week, then cut whatever does not truly need doing | v: self-direction, security | chance: 70
- B | go cynical: do the bare minimum, and save your strength for yourself | habit | v: hedonism, security | chance: 80
- R | walk out in the middle of the shift, and stay away until you feel human | v: self-direction | closed: approval: walking out; backfire: a warning, or the sack | chance: 62
- G | take sick leave and sleep for as long as the body asks | v: security | chance: 75
- W>B | file a formal complaint about the workload, strictly by the book | v: power, security | chance: 50
- U>R | plan a three-month break down to the last detail, then take it | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 68
- B>G | trade the salary for a smaller job and a slower life somewhere quiet | binds | v: security, hedonism | mark: moved away | chance: 72
- R>W | stand up at the next meeting and say what this job is doing to everyone | identity | v: universalism (fairness) | mark: defied an authority | chance: 45
- G>U | spend a week in a cabin with no screens, and let your mind clear | door | v: self-direction | chance: 72
works: {N} rests, and one morning the tiredness is simply gone.
works: Something gives at work, and the weeks get lighter.
fails: {N} keeps going until the body decides instead, and {N} falls ill.
fails: The change costs more than it saves, and the tiredness comes back with interest.

== the anniversary of a death
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: loss, family
horizon: week
roles: dead, parent, sibling, partner
earth: the day someone you loved died comes round again, and the world carries on as if it were any other day
requires: the death of someone close (a parent, partner, child, sibling, grandparent or friend) a year or more ago, and the date, their birthday or a holiday they loved comes round this week
likelier: the death was sudden, or of a child or partner; the first few anniversaries; belonging below 0.4; few other ties; their things still in the house
rarer: many years have passed; a faith and its rites; a family that marks the day together (ties above 0.6)
times: Nearly everyone who has lost someone close, once a year around the date; grief researchers call these anniversary reactions
gap: 0.8-1
scene: The date on the calendar is just a number to everyone else. {N} wakes before the alarm, knowing exactly what day it is.
scene W: Every year on this day {N} lights a candle for {dead}. Someone has to remember properly, and it falls to {N}.
scene U: {N} counts the years since {dead} died and finds the number does not fit: it feels both much longer and much shorter.
scene B: {N} thinks of everything {dead} never got round to, and hears the clock of {Ns} own life ticking louder.
scene R: A song in the shop, the one {dead} always sang, and {N} has to put the basket down and walk out.
scene G: The same blossom is out that was out the week {dead} died. {N} stands under it for a long time.
- W | go to the grave with the family, and keep the day as it should be kept | habit | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 90
- U | write down every memory of them you still have, before it fades | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 90
- B | use the day to make the decision for yourself that you keep putting off | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 78
- R | let yourself cry, loudly, wherever it comes | v: none clear (grief let out) | role: women | chance: 85
- G | sit in silence in a place they loved, and let the grief pass through | v: tradition, universalism (wisdom) | chance: 90
- W>R | start a yearly game in their name with friends, and play their music after | binds | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 79
- U>G | learn to cook their signature dish exactly, from their old notes | v: tradition | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- B>W | chip in for a bench with their name on it, where everyone will see | identity | v: tradition, benevolence | tags: pay:money-.05 | chance: 78
- R>U | go on impulse to the place they died, to make sense of it at last | v: self-direction | chance: 68
- G>B | let the day pass unmarked this year, and keep your strength for the living | v: security | chance: 60
works: The day is hard, and then it is over, and {N} feels lighter for having marked it.
works: Remembering {dead} out loud, {N} laughs for the first time in a long while.
fails: The grief comes back as fresh as the first week, and stays for days.
fails: {N} spends the day alone and wrong-footed, and nobody else seems to remember.

== nothing seems to matter
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 15-110
tone: trouble
life: faith, work, home
horizon: months
roles: friend, partner, an elder
earth: you got what you were working for, or lost it, and now the days look like grey cardboard
requires: meaning below 0.3 for eight weeks or more; or a goal held for years reached or lost within the year (graduation, retirement, the children gone, a cause won or lost) with meaning below 0.45; or a success that brought no rise in satisfaction
likelier: young adult years and old age; an age ending in 9 or 0; within a few years of leaving a faith; ends mostly money and image (much Black in the ends); baseline mood below 0.45
rarer: belonging above 0.6; a faith or community commitment held; children; work felt as a calling (career held, meaning above 0.6)
times: Many people, every several years, after a goal is reached or lost or in a low stretch; about 1 in 5 US adults has a major depressive episode in life (Hasin and colleagues 2018)
gap: 3-8
scene: {N} does everything that needs doing, and none of it seems to weigh anything. At night {N} lies awake asking what it is all for.
scene W: {N} used to know what the duties were for. Now {N} keeps them out of habit, like lamps left burning in an empty house.
scene U: {N} has an answer for every question except the one that keeps coming back: why any of it?
scene B: {N} got what {N} wanted. It sits on the shelf like a trophy, and {N} feels nothing when {N} looks at it.
scene R: Nothing makes {Ns} heart beat faster any more. Not music, not love, not anger. {N} would take any feeling over this.
scene G: {N} feels cut off, like a branch that has come away from the tree and does not know it yet.
- W | turn to a faith, old or new, and keep its practices faithfully | habit | v: tradition | tags: commit:faith | chance: 70
- U | read the philosophers and keep a journal until you have an answer of your own | door | v: self-direction | chance: 65
- B | buy something big and expensive, just to feel something | v: hedonism, power (resources) | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 45
- R | quit something or start something, anything, so long as it is sudden | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 62
- G | stop asking, and live small, slow days close to home until it lifts | v: tradition (humility), security | chance: 68
- W>G | volunteer at the hospice, and sit with people at the end of their lives | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 80
- U>W | study how the people you most admire live, and copy their code | identity | v: conformity, self-direction | chance: 65
- B>U | pay for a course or a therapist, and treat the emptiness like a project | door | v: self-direction | chance: 75
- R>B | pick the fiercest rival you can find, and set out to beat them | v: achievement, stimulation | mark: made an enemy | chance: 62
- G>R | sleep out alone on a hill under the stars until something stirs | door | body: light | v: stimulation, universalism (nature) | chance: 65
works: Slowly, without {N} noticing when, the days take on weight again.
works: {N} finds one thing that matters, and it is enough to start with.
fails: The emptiness hangs on through the season, and {N} stops expecting it to lift.
fails: What {N} tried feels hollow too, and {N} gives it up.

== homesick
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: home, family
horizon: months
roles: parent, grandparent, sibling, friend
earth: a new room in a new place, and a pang every evening when you think of the kitchen at home
requires: moved away from home within the last three months (a camp, boarding school, university, a job abroad, migration, a care home), with ties back home above 0.5 and belonging in the new place below 0.4
likelier: a first time away; strong family ties; a new place very unlike home; few new friends yet; holidays and family birthdays; reactivity above 1.2
rarer: earlier time away; quick new friendships; plenty of sport and activity; a partner who came along
times: Most people, a few times in a life: camp, university, a job far away, a care home; for most it fades within months (estimate)
gap: 2-6
scene: Every evening around six, when the light goes, {N} thinks of the kitchen at home and the voices in it, and the new room feels very far away.
scene W: At home {N} knew where everything went and who would be at the table. Here every day has to be worked out from nothing.
scene U: {N} keeps catching small wrongnesses: the bread tastes different, the birds sound different, the light falls at the wrong angle.
scene B: {N} came here to get on, and knows it. But nobody here knows {Ns} name yet, and that is harder than {N} expected.
scene R: A smell of cooking in the corridor, almost like the dish {grandparent} makes, and {N} has to sit down on the stairs.
scene G: {N} feels like a plant moved to a new pot, roots all bunched up, not yet sure the soil will take.
- W | tell the warden or the tutor you are struggling, and take the help on offer | v: security, conformity | chance: 77
- U | learn the new place properly: map it, read about it, find what works | door | v: self-direction, security | chance: 85
- B | remind yourself what this place is a step towards, and push through | v: achievement | chance: 82
- R | say yes to every party and every invitation, starting tonight | door | v: stimulation | chance: 82
- G | pack it in and go home | v: security, tradition | mark: turned down a chance | closed: approval: quitting halfway; backfire: the place is lost, and the money with it | chance: 58
- W>U | enrol in the local language or orientation course, and go to every class | v: self-direction, conformity | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
- U>B | work out who here could be useful, and make yourself known to them | v: power, achievement | chance: 72
- B>R | talk your way into a cheap lift home with someone driving that way | v: hedonism | chance: 78
- R>G | share the food and music from home with the whole corridor, tonight | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 90
- G>W | find the people here from where you come from, and keep the old holidays together | habit | v: tradition, conformity | mark: made a friend | chance: 78
works: One evening {N} realises the pang did not come, and the new place has started to feel like a place.
works: {N} finds a corner of home in the new town, and the rest becomes bearable.
fails: The pang gets worse each week, and {N} can think of little else.
fails: {N} leaves too early and regrets it, or stays too long and is miserable.

== anger that keeps building
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: trouble
life: work, family, community
horizon: months
roles: rival, boss, sibling, a neighbour
earth: the same person keeps doing the same thing, and every time it happens the heat rises a little higher
requires: the same person or situation has slighted, blocked or wronged the person three or more times within the last three months with no apology, and stress above 1 with peace below 0.4
likelier: health below 0.5 (pain, tiredness); much Red or Black in the color history; reactivity above 1.2; an old history with this person; the wrong touches someone the person protects
rarer: steadiness above 1; ties with the one who did it above 0.6; time and space to cool off; much White or Blue restraint in the color history
times: Most people, a few times a year at this pitch; milder anger comes several times a week for most (Averill's diary studies)
gap: 0-0.5
scene: It has happened again. {N} says nothing, smiles even, but the heat that has been building for weeks climbs another notch.
scene W: There are rules for how people treat each other, and {rival} breaks them every time. Someone ought to make it stop.
scene U: {N} lies awake rehearsing the argument, every line of it, and wins it every time in the dark.
scene B: {N} keeps a careful tally of every slight. One day the account will be settled, with interest.
scene R: {Ns} jaw aches from clenching. One more time, just one more, and {N} knows it is all going to come out.
scene G: Pressure builds under the ground for a long time before the mountain moves. {N} can feel it building now.
- W | write a formal complaint that sets out every incident with dates | v: conformity, security | chance: 65
- U | count to ten, step away, and come back only when your head is cool | habit | v: self-direction, conformity | chance: 85
- B | wait patiently, and pay them back when they least expect it | v: power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: revenge; backfire: it escalates, and both sides suffer | chance: 66
- R | have it out with them, face to face, right now | v: self-direction, power | chance: 68
- G | forgive them in your own heart, and let the thing go | v: benevolence, tradition (humility) | chance: 68
- W>B | report them for every small rule they break, until they are punished | v: power, conformity | closed: approval: a vendetta by the rulebook; backfire: seen as petty, and the rules turn on the one who used them | chance: 45
- U>R | write a cutting letter, every word chosen, and send it while still angry | v: power, self-direction | chance: 50
- B>G | cut them out of your life without a word, and let them wonder why | v: security | mark: made an enemy | chance: 80
- R>W | lose your temper in public, so everyone finally sees what they have done | identity | v: universalism (fairness) | chance: 42
- G>U | sit with the anger until you see what it is really about | v: self-direction | chance: 72
works: The anger finds its way out, and the air clears.
works: {rival} backs off, and {N} sleeps properly for the first time in weeks.
fails: It all comes out at the worst possible moment, in front of the wrong people.
fails: The anger turns inward and sours, and {N} carries it around for months.

== a craving that keeps calling
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 13-110
tone: mixed
life: body, leisure
horizon: week
roles: friend, partner
earth: a drink, a bet, a cigarette, something sweet, a screen: the thing your body has learned to want, calling at the usual hour
requires: an act flagged habit around a pleasure (drink, gambling, smoking, sweets, a screen) chosen eight or more times within the last year, and a cue this week (the usual hour, a place, a smell, a friend who shares it); or a day without it after many; stress above 1 makes it stronger
likelier: stress above 1.5; tiredness; the evening after a day of hard self-control; much Red or Black in the color history; friends who share the habit
rarer: a place with none of the cues; an absorbing goal; good sleep; a partner or child who would be hurt by it
times: Nearly everyone with a habit, most weeks; about 1 in 9 US adults still smoke cigarettes (CDC 2021)
scene: It is the usual hour. {Ns} hands know where it is before {Ns} mind has decided anything.
scene W: {N} made a rule about this, and kept it for nine days. Now the rule feels thin as paper.
scene U: {N} watches the wanting rise like a line on a chart: the trigger, the climb, the peak. Knowing the pattern does not make it smaller.
scene B: {N} has earned this. After the day {N} has had, who is anyone to say no?
scene R: The wanting is everywhere, in the mouth, in the hands, in the chest. Just once, just now.
scene G: The body wants what the body wants. {N} listens, and wonders whether it is hunger or habit talking.
- W | keep your rule, and tell someone you trust that you kept it | v: conformity | chance: 82
- U | time the craving for twenty minutes, knowing it will peak and fall | v: self-direction, security | chance: 82
- B | give in, but do it where nobody will see | habit | v: hedonism | mark: hid a wrong | chance: 65
- R | give in fully, and enjoy every second of it | habit | v: hedonism | chance: 62
- G | go for a walk until it passes, the way weather passes | v: security | chance: 90
- W>R | swap it for a weekly game or night out with friends who never touch it | v: hedonism, conformity | chance: 75
- U>G | learn what your body is really asking for, and give it that instead | v: security, self-direction | chance: 75
- B>W | bet a friend real money that you can quit for three months | binds | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 70
- R>U | throw out every bottle, packet or app in the house, tonight | v: security, self-direction | self_control: + | chance: 88
- G>B | stay close to the friends who share it, so there is always some to hand | v: hedonism, conformity | closed: approval: keeping the company that feeds the habit; backfire: found out, and trusted less | chance: 45
works: The wanting rises, peaks and passes, and {N} is still standing.
works: {N} finds something that answers the craving without the cost.
fails: Once becomes three times, and the evening is gone.
fails: {N} holds out for days, then gives in harder than ever.

== trapped by a promise
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 16-110
tone: trouble
life: love, family, work
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, boss, an elder
earth: you gave your word years ago, a contract, a vow, a promise to stay or to care, and now it holds you like a fence
requires: an act flagged binds (a vow, a debt, a contract, a promise to care for someone) or a commitment held for a year or more, and autonomy below 0.35 for eight weeks or more; or a plan to leave it blocked again within the year
likelier: much Red or Black in the color history (self-direction and stimulation ranked high); money below 0.25; dependence on one person; family or community against leaving; a caring role
rarer: savings; a life and friends outside the promise (ties above 0.6); meaning found in the role (meaning above 0.6); much White in the ends
times: Many people, at some stretch of life, for months or years at a time: a marriage, a mortgage, a parent's care (estimate)
gap: 2-4
scene: {N} said yes, years ago, and meant it. Now the promise sits at the centre of every day, and {N} has started counting the bars.
scene W: A promise is a promise. {N} repeats it like a prayer, and the prayer is wearing thin.
scene U: {N} reads the old agreement again, line by line, looking for the clause that was never really there.
scene B: {N} was young and did not know what it would cost. Somebody else is getting the better end of this deal.
scene R: {N} catches themselves at the window, looking at the road, and the wanting to just walk is so strong it hurts.
scene G: Some roots grow round a stone and cannot let go without tearing. {N} wonders which of them is the stone.
