rarer: a role others rely on; a close circle; public standing; much Red in the color history
times: Many people, a stretch every year or two; about 1 in 2 US adults report loneliness (US Surgeon General 2023)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: {N} says something at the table. Nobody answers, and the talk flows on round {N} like water round a stone.
scene W: {N} has done the right thing for years, quietly, and nobody has once said they noticed. {N} begins to wonder whether it counts.
scene U: {N} starts to keep count: how many times {N} spoke this week, and how many times anyone replied.
scene B: Nobody listens to someone who has nothing they want. {N} sees that clearly now, and does not like what it means.
scene R: {N} wants to stand on the table and shout, just to see whether anyone would look up.
scene G: {N} feels like an old tree at the edge of the field. Everyone walks past it, and nobody remembers who planted it.
- W | make yourself useful to everyone, and trust that it will be noticed in time | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 65
- U | write what you think every week, in a letter to the paper or online | habit | identity | v: self-direction | chance: 68
- B | make yourself the one who holds the keys, the money or the list | binds | v: power | chance: 80
- R | get up at the next open mic or talent night, and make the room listen | v: stimulation, power (face) | chance: 55
- G | stop trying to be heard, and turn to the garden, the dog and the quiet | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 55
- W>B | stand for election to the council or committee, so your voice has to count | identity | v: power, achievement | chance: 48
- U>R | learn to tell stories so well that the room goes quiet when you start | v: achievement, stimulation | mark: learned a skill | chance: 68
- B>G | drop the crowd that never listens, and keep only the two or three who do | v: security, benevolence | chance: 85
- R>W | tell the whole table, there and then, what it feels like to be ignored | v: benevolence | chance: 75
- G>U | sit back and watch them all closely; the quiet one sees the most | v: self-direction | chance: 58
works: Someone turns, at last, and asks {N} what {N} thinks, and waits for the answer.
works: {N} finds a place where {Ns} voice carries.
fails: The silence round {N} grows, and {N} stops speaking at all.
fails: The attempt to be seen goes badly, and now {N} is noticed for the wrong thing.

== a sense of injustice
tier: inner
stages: juvenile+
age: 12-110
tone: mixed
life: community, work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, friend, a neighbour
earth: a rule bent for the powerful and enforced on everyone else, and you cannot stop thinking about it
requires: the person or their group treated worse than others for no fair reason within the last month (passed over, underpaid, singled out, a rule enforced on them and waived for the powerful), or news of an injustice touching the ends the person holds most; and the feeling has not faded after four weeks
likelier: much White in the ends (rules should bind everyone); the unfairness falls on a group the person belongs to; outlook above 0.45 (change looks possible); juvenile and young adult years
rarer: the person gains from the arrangement; outlook below 0.3 (nothing ever changes); much Green acceptance in the color history
times: Most people, about once a year at this strength, over something done to them or news that touches what they hold dear (estimate)
gap: 0.8-1
scene: It is not even {Ns} own business, strictly speaking. But {N} cannot stop thinking about it, and every time it comes back {Ns} hands go tight.
scene W: There is a rule, and it was bent for the people who could afford it. If it does not bind everyone, it binds no one.
scene U: {N} lays out the facts side by side: who got what, and why. The numbers do not add up, and {N} wants to know who made them.
scene B: The people at the top look after their own. {N} has always known it. What galls is how openly they do it.
scene R: {Ns} blood is up. {N} wants to march into the office and say it to their faces, right now.
scene G: When one tree takes all the light, the ones beneath it wither. {N} has seen it in the woods, and now sees it here.
- W | expose the one responsible in public, and keep at it until they lose their post | v: universalism (fairness), power | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: a shaming campaign; backfire: the crowd turns, or a suit for libel | chance: 45
- U | document everything, and take it through every proper channel, step by step | identity | v: universalism (fairness), conformity | chance: 65
- B | get yourself a seat at the table where such rules are made | v: power | chance: 40
- R | speak out at the next meeting and name names | identity | v: universalism (fairness), stimulation | mark: defied an authority | chance: 78
- G | accept that the world has always worked this way, and tend your own corner | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 65
- W>R | rally everyone who feels the same, and protest it together, loudly | v: universalism, stimulation | chance: 78
- U>G | find the old law or charter that protects your people, and hold them to it | v: universalism, tradition | chance: 50
- B>W | quietly help yourself to what you are owed, and say nothing | v: power (resources), universalism (fairness) | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: theft; backfire: caught, and the unfairness turned on the taker | chance: 78
- R>U | keep asking the awkward question, loudly, until someone has to answer | v: self-direction, universalism | chance: 68
- G>B | close ranks with your own kind, and stop trusting anyone outside | identity | v: security, tradition | chance: 75
works: The unfairness is put right, or at least named out loud, and {N} can sleep again.
works: Others turn out to feel the same, and {N} is no longer alone with it.
fails: Nothing changes, and the powerful carry on as before.
fails: {N} pays for speaking up, and the people responsible do not.

== feeling old
tier: inner
stages: adult+
age: 38-110
tone: mixed
life: body, aging, work
horizon: months
roles: boss, child, partner, friend
earth: a stranger offers you their seat on the bus, and you catch your own face in the window
requires: felt age catches up with real age: health below 0.6 with something the body used to do now lost, or a round birthday from 40 (40, 50, 60, 70, 80), or within the year a first grandchild, a younger boss or the death of a friend of the same age
likelier: health below 0.5; retirement within two years; a job or circle that prizes youth; few friends of other ages; outlook below 0.4
rarer: health above 0.8; friends of every age; much Green in the color history (ageing accepted); an active role others rely on
times: Nearly everyone from midlife on, every few years; adults over 40 tend to feel about a fifth younger than they are (Rubin and Berntsen 2006)
gap: 3-6
scene: A young stranger offers {N} a seat on the bus. {N} sits, thanks them, and catches {Ns} own face in the dark window.
scene W: {N} still does everything the way it should be done, only slower now, and wonders how long before the young ones take it over.
scene U: {N} notices the small print has got smaller and the stairs longer, and keeps a quiet list of what has changed.
scene B: {boss} is half {Ns} age. {N} knows what the young think of the old, and does not intend to be put out to grass.
scene R: Inside, {N} is still nineteen. The knees disagree, and {N} is furious with them.
scene G: Every season leaves its ring in the wood. {N} counts them in the mirror, and is not sure yet whether to mind.
- W | book every check-up, and follow the doctor's advice to the letter | habit | v: security, conformity | chance: 85
- U | learn something completely new, to prove the mind is still young | door | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- B | dye the grey, buy younger clothes, and knock a few years off your age | v: power (face), hedonism | chance: 72
- R | take up a fast, hard sport and train like a teenager | habit | body: heavy | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 60
- G | accept the lines on your face as the record of a life | v: tradition (humility) | chance: 85
- W>G | start mentoring the young ones at work or in the club | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 85
- U>W | write down all you know about the work, so it is still done right later | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 90
- B>U | pay for the treatments and gadgets that keep body and mind sharp | v: achievement, security | chance: 62
- R>B | refuse to step aside, and fight anyone who suggests you should | v: power | chance: 50
- G>R | go back to the place you were young, and swim in the same cold river | body: light | v: stimulation, tradition | chance: 85
works: {N} makes a kind of peace with the years, and finds they have given as much as they took.
works: The body answers better than {N} feared, and the mirror stops mattering so much.
fails: Every small loss feels like the start of a long slide, and {N} broods on it.
fails: {N} pushes too hard to stay young, and pays for it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- longings and urges (mixed)

== wanting to be noticed
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 12-110
tone: mixed
life: school, work, family
horizon: week
roles: sibling, rival, boss, a teacher
earth: everyone else's name gets called, and you want, just once, for the room to turn and look at you
