gap: 0-0.5
scene: Everyone is looking at someone else again. {N} feels the wish rise, bright and a little ashamed: just once, look at me.
scene W: {N} has done everything asked, and done it well. Surely someone ought to say so.
scene U: {N} notices exactly who gets attention here and why: who speaks first, who speaks loudest, who gets the last word.
scene B: Attention is a kind of currency. {N} has noticed that {rival} has plenty of it, and {N} has none.
scene R: {N} wants to sing, to shout, to turn a cartwheel in the middle of the room, anything to make them all look.
scene G: The bright flowers get the bees. {N} wonders, for the first time, whether to be bright.
- W | volunteer for the job at the front: reading, leading, speaking for the group | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 75
- U | learn one thing better than anyone around, and wait to be asked | habit | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 68
